    "Reviewed all eighteen contexts, prompts, accepted responses and explanations against the actual published library. Retained seventeen; substituted an existing unambiguous future-form item for the exposed plural response.",
    "Use one reading and one language-use sample per band where fresh items allow; a mixed result uses the third. No translation or answer-bearing feedback until the assessment is over.",
    "The gap replacement is strongly scaffolded, and several advanced items have easy distractors. These are practice-range probes, not empirical CEFR classification. Advanced success must not imply productive ability, listening, speaking or a certified level.",
    "B1 tide-song explanation overstates what the passage explicitly says: future contribution is a reasonable inference, not an explicit purpose quote. Do not show this explanation during placement. Existing source activity remains unchanged in this update."
